5. Rewrite this using modern Java 16+ pattern matching:
if (obj instanceof String) {
    String s = (String) obj;
    System.out.println(s.length());
}
if (obj instanceof Integer) {
    Integer i = (Integer) obj;
    System.out.println(i * 2);
}

items.a:
Modern rewrite:
if (obj instanceof String s) {
    System.out.println(s.length());
} else if (obj instanceof Integer i) {
    System.out.println(i * 2);
}
The pattern matching syntax combines the instanceof check and the variable binding in one expression. No separate cast needed. The bound variables s and i are automatically the correct type within their respective blocks. This is more concise, eliminates the redundant explicit cast, and makes ClassCastException impossible in these code paths.

